// ISCC-NBS color-name taxonomy: 13 / 29 / 267 terms across three levels.
//
// Transcribed from NBS Special Publication 440, "Color: Universal Language and
// Dictionary of Names" (Kelly & Judd, 1976) via bstreiff/iscc-nbs-colors (CC0-1.0).
//
// 'term' alone is NOT unique -- 'Pink', 'Red', 'Green' and so on name both a level-1
// and a level-2 category, and 'White'/'Black' exist at all three levels. The node key
// is therefore the pair (level, term). 'number' is the ISCC-NBS number, also unique
// only within its level.
//
// Every category except the 13 at level 1 gets one :BROADER edge to its parent one
// level up, so the hierarchy is walkable with [:BROADER*].

